# Plan: Persist Loyalty Rank with PostgreSQL and Redis Cache

We will migrate the simulated in-memory `LoyaltyDb` in `Discount.API` to use **PostgreSQL** for persistent writing (long-term database) and **Redis** for high-performance reading (caching).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - We will create a new PostgreSQL database named `discountdb` to isolate the loyalty data.
> - We will use the built-in .NET Aspire integrations (`Aspire.Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL` and `Aspire.StackExchange.Redis`) to simplify setup.

